 "design": "R6 how loud the item noise can get before the estimator stops recovering the ratio.\n\nDesign fixed before running (2026-09-16, written 17:45 EDT). The two populations this paper simulates sit\nat item noise of 0.73 and 1.45, which are the values the margin and accuracy batteries imply. A reader\napplying the method to a smaller battery, a harder task, or fewer items per benchmark will sit further\nout, and the cross-half construction has to divide a shrinking signal by a growing denominator. Nothing\nwe have run says where that stops working, and the accuracy case at 1.45 already covers less well inside a\nsingle band than the margin case at 0.73.\nThis run sweeps the item noise over 0.25, 0.5, 0.73, 1.0, 1.45, 2.0 and 3.0 at the full 125-cell design,\nholding the true ratio at 1.2446, with 4,000 replicates each. It reports coverage, the exclusion rate and\nthe median width, so a reader can see both where the interval fails and where it merely becomes useless\nthrough width. Seed 20260976 keeps the draws distinct.\n",
